{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1935","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1935","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1935\",\"parent_revision\":\"1d1d2de1308c466414947d86521f6c2e7e159f130903aba2ef5f66c6aba7be9a\",\"root_revision\":\"1d1d2de1308c466414947d86521f6c2e7e159f130903aba2ef5f66c6aba7be9a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-05-08\\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add plugin manifest reference cross-check hook (catch dangling skill/command/hook references)** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/wrkflw.md \u2014 pattern: Workflow Validation with Composite Action Input Cross-Checking (line 70)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-25\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-26)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\n\\n| Input | Condition | Notes |\\n|-------|-----------|-------|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Cross-check plugin.json path references against disk; fail on dangling references |\\n| Scope boundaries | PARTIAL | Which fields to check is derivable; whether to parse hook command strings for paths is not specified |\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | Pre-commit hook pattern in .pre-commit-config.yaml; check_agent_auto_discovery.py is the direct model |\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | All relevant scripts, manifests, and hooks infrastructure present |\\n| Trigger pattern | PARTIAL | plugin.json-only vs component file deletions not specified |\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen a developer commits a plugin.json that references a path such as ./skills/my-skill or ./agents/my-agent.md that does not exist on disk, the pre-commit hook exits non-zero and prints a human-readable message identifying the plugin name, the field, and the missing path. The commit is blocked. When all referenced paths exist on disk, the hook exits 0 and produces no output.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nA pre-commit hook script check_manifest_references.py in plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/ registered in .pre-commit-config.yaml that:\\n\\n- Accepts one or more plugin.json paths as positional arguments (pass_filenames: true)\\n- For each manifest, checks that every path value in skills, agents, commands, hooks, and mcpServers fields resolves to an existing file or directory on disk\\n- Prints a structured error per violation and exits non-zero when any violations are found\\n- Exits 0 with no output when all references resolve\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Running `uv run plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/check_manifest_references.py plugins/some-plugin/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` exits non-zero and prints the missing path when skills, agents, commands, hooks, or mcpServers contains a path that does not exist on disk.\\n2. Running the same command against a plugin.json with all paths present exits 0 with no output.\\n3. The hook is registered in .pre-commit-config.yaml with `files: ^plugins/.*\\\\.claude-plugin/plugin\\\\.json$` and `pass_filenames: true`.\\n4. Running `uv run prek run --files plugins/some-plugin/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` with a broken reference causes the check-manifest-references hook to fail and display the violation.\\n5. Paths in skills, agents, commands are verified to exist; the script does not attempt to parse hook command strings or mcpServer args array entries for embedded paths (those use runtime substitution).\\n6. Invalid JSON in plugin.json causes a clear error message and non-zero exit.\\n7. A plugin.json using only auto-discovery (no skills/agents/commands keys declared) passes the check with exit 0.\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- Should inline hooks object values (not a file path string) be silently skipped, or flagged as a style warning?\\n- Should mcpServer args entries containing absolute paths be verified for existence, or is all mcpServer path resolution explicitly out of scope?\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/check_agent_auto_discovery.py \u2014 direct implementation model |\\n| Prior work | plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/auto_sync_manifests.py \u2014 field taxonomy reference |\\n| Prior work | .pre-commit-config.yaml \u2014 hook registration template |\\n| Prior work | .claude/rules/plugin-json.md \u2014 authoritative field list and path rules |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:hooks-guide |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:plugin-creator |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 all prerequisite infrastructure is already in place\\n- Blocks: None identified\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\nNone. All required inputs are AVAILABLE or DERIVABLE from the existing codebase.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 check_agent_auto_discovery.py is an exact structural template. Estimated scope: one new Python script (~100-150 lines), two documentation updates, one .pre-commit-config.yaml entry.\\n\\n### Fields to Check (from .claude/rules/plugin-json.md)\\n\\n| Field | Check type |\\n|-------|------------|\\n| skills | Each entry resolves to a directory containing SKILL.md, or to a direct file path |\\n| agents | Each entry resolves to a .md file on disk |\\n| commands | Each entry resolves to a .md file on disk |\\n| hooks | String value: verify the referenced .json file exists; object value (inline): skip |\\n| mcpServers | String value: verify the referenced .json file exists; object value with command field: skip (runtime command) |\\n\\nAny path value containing `${...}` substitution variables must be skipped \u2014 runtime-resolved.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/check_manifest_references.py | Create new hook script (Python 3.11+, stdlib-only PEP 723, same pattern as check_agent_auto_discovery.py) |\\n| .pre-commit-config.yaml | Add hook entry under local hooks block |\\n| plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/CLAUDE.md | Add row to Scripts Overview table |\\n| plugins/plugin-creator/CLAUDE.md | Add hook to Scripts section inventory |\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a developer committing changes to a plugin, I want the pre-commit hook to catch plugin.json references to files that do not exist on disk, so that a bad commit never ships a manifest with dangling paths that silently make components invisible or break plugin loading.\\n\\nAs an agent grooming or creating a plugin, I want immediate feedback when a plugin.json skill, agent, command, hook, or mcpServer path is wrong, so the issue is caught at commit time rather than discovered at session startup.\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\n`./.pre-commit-config.yaml` lines 127-142 runs `auto_sync_manifests.py` and `check_agent_auto_discovery.py` against plugin manifests. Composite-action-style cross-checking between a manifest's declared inputs/agents and the files those references resolve to is partial: `check_agent_auto_discovery.py` exists for agents but no analogous check exists for the cross-product of `commands:`, `skills:`, `hooks:` references in `plugin.json` vs the files those entries point at.\\n\\nA typo in `plugin.json` referencing a skill that does not exist on disk is not caught at pre-commit; the failure surfaces only when a user tries to invoke the dead reference.\\n\\nThis mirrors wrkflw's \\\"composite action input cross-checking\\\" \u2014 the pattern of validating that a manifest's declared inputs map to real, resolvable definitions on disk.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\n`./.pre-commit-config.yaml` lines 127-142 runs `auto_sync_manifests.py` and `check_agent_auto_discovery.py` against plugin manifests. Composite-action-style cross-checking between a manifest's declared inputs/agents and the files those references resolve to is partial: `check_agent_auto_discovery.py` exists for agents but no analogous check exists for the cross-product of `commands:`, `skills:`, `hooks:` references in `plugin.json` vs the files those entries point at.\\n\\nA typo in `plugin.json` referencing a skill that does not exist on disk is not caught at pre-commit; the failure surfaces only when a user tries to invoke the dead reference.\\n\\nThis mirrors wrkflw's \\\"composite action input cross-checking\\\" \u2014 the pattern of validating that a manifest's declared inputs map to real, resolvable definitions on disk.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA new `scripts/check_plugin_manifest_references.py` hook validates that every entry under `commands:`, `skills:`, `agents:`, `hooks:` in `plugin.json` resolves to a real file/directory. The hook exits 1 with the unresolved reference and the manifest line number when any reference is dangling.\\n\\nWired into `./.pre-commit-config.yaml` alongside the existing `auto-sync-manifests` and `check-agent-auto-discovery` hooks, with `files: ^plugins/.*/\\\\\\\\.claude-plugin/plugin\\\\\\\\.json$`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nInject `\\\"skills\\\": [\\\"does-not-exist\\\"]` into a plugin's `plugin.json`. Run `uv run prek run --hook check-plugin-manifest-references --files plugins/<plugin>/.claude-plugin/plugin.json`. Hook exits non-zero with message naming `does-not-exist` and the JSON path. Remove the bad reference and re-run \u2014 hook exits 0.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nResearch entry: `./research/developer-tools/wrkflw.md`, \\\"Workflow Validation with Exit Codes\\\" section, specifically the \\\"composite action input cross-checking\\\" mechanism.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"fcdae706f33eae182f1cd43fee9d1c92c1bc3b0a156fa22851f24df646ce9efd\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCU5eA\"}"}